  "final_answer": "I found the answer! In the Quick Facts section of Cornell University's website, I can see:\n\n**Cornell University Information:**\n- Location: Ithaca, New York\n- Founded: 1865\n- **Undergraduate Students: 16,138**\n- Graduate and Professional Students: 10,423\n- Faculty: 3,025\n- Nobel Laureates: 52\n- $425M+ undergraduate grant aid\n\nLet me also verify the connection between ArXiv and Cornell by going back to confirm the source. Based on what I learned earlier, \"arXiv was founded by Paul Ginsparg in 1991 and, after decades of being hosted at Cornell University, was established as an independent nonprofit organization in 2026.\"\n\n## Final Answer:\n\n**The university that maintains and manages ArXiv is Cornell University.**\n\nAccording to Cornell University's website (cornell.edu), there are currently **16,138 undergraduate students** at Cornell University. This figure was found in the \"Quick Facts\" section of the About Cornell > Overview page.",
